# Pin this checkout to the gcloud configuration that owns its infrastructure.
#
# The host, the artifact registry and the logs all live in project `matthewc`
# under matthew.finn.carroll@gmail.com. Without this, a shell here inherits
# whatever configuration happens to be active globally — on 2026-09-14 that was
# eb-zoom-automation (admin@ecobytes.ca / pl-cg-integration), and every gcloud
# call mid-incident failed with PERMISSION_DENIED on `matthewc` while
# production was down. The directory should decide the identity, not the
# order in which things were last run.
#
# Footgun, per cupe-5430-soc/.envrc: `gcloud auth login` and `gcloud config set`
# act on the ACTIVE configuration, which this file pins. Name it explicitly for
# any auth or config change, or you will silently rewrite this one:
#     CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME=matthewc gcloud auth login
#
# Verify with:  gcloud config configurations list
export CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME="matthewc"
